---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import KeyTakeaways from '../components/KeyTakeaways.astro';
import DisclaimerBox from '../components/DisclaimerBox.astro';
import CrisisBanner from '../components/CrisisBanner.astro';
import TableOfContents from '../components/TableOfContents.astro';
import '../styles/styleguide.css';
const colors = [
  { name: 'white', purpose: 'Main page background' },
  { name: 'sand', purpose: 'Callouts and warm surfaces' },
  { name: 'sand-soft', purpose: 'Quiet section backgrounds' },
  { name: 'ink', purpose: 'Reading text and headings' },
  { name: 'muted', purpose: 'Supporting text' },
  { name: 'link', purpose: 'Links, controls, and focus rings' },
  { name: 'link-hover', purpose: 'Hovered links and controls' },
  { name: 'border', purpose: 'Decorative dividers' },
];
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'colors', text: 'The color palette' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'type', text: 'Type and reading' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'controls', text: 'Links, buttons, and focus' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'reading-components', text: 'Reading and support components' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'references', text: 'References' },
];
---

<Base title="Styleguide" description="The internal design reference for Psychology Blog: color tokens, readable typography, controls, and article components." noindex>
  <div class="container narrow styleguide-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Internal design reference</p>
      <h1>A quiet foundation for reading.</h1>
      <p>Typography, color, and useful components for a calm, accessible reading experience. This reference page is excluded from search indexing.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="styleguide-contents">
      <TableOfContents headings={headings} mode="desktop" />
      <TableOfContents headings={headings} mode="mobile" />
    </div>
    <section class="styleguide-section" aria-labelledby="colors">
      <h2 id="colors">The color palette</h2>
      <p>Use the named tokens from the shared stylesheet. Light borders add structure; teal marks interactive controls.</p>
      <dl class="swatch-grid">
        {colors.map((color) => <div class="swatch-item"><div class:list={['swatch', `swatch-${color.name}`]} aria-hidden="true"></div><dt><code>--{color.name}</code></dt><dd>{color.purpose}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section class="styleguide-section prose" aria-labelledby="type">
      <h2 id="type">Type and reading</h2>
      <p>Arial is the reading font. The body uses 18px text and a line height of 1.7. Paragraphs stay near 70 characters wide.</p>
      <h3>A heading introduces one clear idea.</h3>
      <p>You do not need to have the right words for a feeling before you can begin to explore it. A short read can offer a starting point, with room to pause.</p>
      <h4>A smaller heading adds useful detail.</h4>
      <p><strong>Bold text adds emphasis.</strong> <em>Italics add a quieter emphasis.</em> Use both sparingly so the main thought stays easy to follow.</p>
      <p class="fine-print">Supporting information stays readable and uses the muted text token.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="styleguide-section" aria-labelledby="controls">
      <h2 id="controls">Links, buttons, and focus</h2>
      <p>Use a keyboard to move through these controls. Each has a visible teal focus ring and enough space to select it.</p>
      <div class="styleguide-actions"><a class="button" href="/start-here/">Start here</a><a class="button secondary" href="/topics/">Browse topics</a><a class="text-link" href="/blog/">Read all articles</a></div>
      <p class="prose">A link within a paragraph is always underlined, such as <a href="/editorial-policy/">our editorial policy</a>.</p>
      <form class="styleguide-form" action="/search/" method="get">
        <label for="styleguide-search">Try a labelled search field</label>
        <input id="styleguide-search" name="q" type="search" placeholder="For example, sleep" />
        <button type="submit">Search articles</button>
      </form>
    </section>
    <section class="styleguide-section" aria-labelledby="reading-components">
      <h2 id="reading-components">Reading and support components</h2>
      <p>Takeaways help a reader decide where to begin. Support information stays clear and does not interrupt reading.</p>
      <KeyTakeaways items={['A short summary gives readers a clear starting point.', 'General education cannot replace individual professional care.', 'Support resources remain one click away.']} id="styleguide-takeaways" />
      <DisclaimerBox />
      <CrisisBanner />
    </section>
    <section class="styleguide-section prose" aria-labelledby="references">
      <h2 id="references">References</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/accessibility/">accessibility statement</a> describes our WCAG 2.2 AA target and current verification limits. The automated token contrast check is available with <code>npm run check:contrast</code>.</p>
      <p>These components demonstrate presentation and do not establish clinical, legal, or accessibility certification.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
